CORENAV
Unified System Navigation Platform
Specification v1.0 Draft
License: GPLv3

MISSION

CoreNav is a modular system navigation platform that
unifies:

* File Management
* Project Management
* Terminal Access
* System Administration
* Plugin Ecosystems
* Security Operations
* Device Management
* Workspace Management

into a single interface.

CoreNav is not merely a file explorer.

CoreNav serves as a unified navigation layer for the
entire operating system.

==================================================
ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLES

1. Everything Is Navigable

Files
Directories
Projects
Archives
Devices
Services
Processes
Containers
Virtual Machines
Network Resources
Cloud Resources
Repositories

shall be accessible through a unified navigation model.

⸻

2. One Backend, Multiple Interfaces

All functionality shall be accessible through:

* GUI
* TUI
* CLI

No feature shall be restricted to a single interface
unless technically impossible.

All interfaces shall share:

* Backend APIs
* Permission Systems
* Plugin Systems
* Workspace Systems

⸻

3. Keyboard First

Every operation shall be accessible through:

* Keyboard Shortcuts
* Command Palette
* CLI Commands

No operation shall require a mouse.

All shortcuts shall be user configurable.

⸻

4. Modular By Default

All major subsystems shall support plugins.

Core functionality shall remain lightweight.

Features may be enabled, disabled, installed, or
removed without affecting unrelated systems.

